  "content": {
    "id": "p5-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Compare the expansions of $(x+5)(x+2)$ and $(x-2)(x-5)$.\nWhat's the same and what's different?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Both have an $x^2$ term and constant term $10$. Their $x$ coefficients have equal magnitude and opposite signs: $7$ and $-7$.",
      "worked": "$\\begin{aligned}(x+5)(x+2)&=x^2+2x+5x+10\\\\&=x^2+7x+10\\\\(x-2)(x-5)&=x^2-5x-2x+10\\\\&=x^2-7x+10\\end{aligned}$\nBoth have an $x^2$ coefficient of $1$ and constant term $10$. The $x$ coefficients are $7$ and $-7$, so only the sign of the $x$ term differs.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
